## 🧱 Part 2: Generating Larger Primes in MATLAB (Without Symbolic Math Toolbox)

MATLAB does **not have built-in functions** for generating large random primes, but we can implement a **probabilistic primality test** like **Miller-Rabin** to generate large primes.

### ✅ Miller-Rabin Primality Test (MATLAB Implementation)

```matlab
function isPrime = isprime_miller_rabin(n, k)
% Miller-Rabin primality test
% n: number to test
% k: number of rounds (higher = more accurate)

if n <= 1
    isPrime = false;
    return;
elseif n <= 3
    isPrime = true;
    return;
elseif mod(n, 2) == 0
    isPrime = false;
    return;
end

% Write n-1 as d*2^s
d = n - 1;
s = 0;
while mod(d, 2) == 0
    d = d / 2;
    s = s + 1;
end

% Test for k rounds
for i = 1:k
    a = 2 + floor((n - 4) * rand());
    x = power_mod(a, d, n);
    if x == 1 || x == n - 1
        continue;
    end
    for j = 1:s-1
        x = power_mod(x, 2, n);
        if x == n - 1
            break;
        end
    end
    if x ~= n - 1
        isPrime = false;
        return;
    end
end
isPrime = true;
end
```

### ✅ Modular Exponentiation (Power Modulo) Without Symbolic Math Toolbox

```matlab
function result = power_mod(base, exponent, modulus)
% Efficient modular exponentiation using binary exponentiation
result = 1;
base = mod(base, modulus);
while exponent > 0
    if mod(exponent, 2) == 1
        result = mod(result * base, modulus);
    end
    base = mod(base * base, modulus);
    exponent = floor(exponent / 2);
end
end
```

### ✅ Generate a Large Random Prime (e.g., 1024-bit)

```matlab
function p = generate_large_prime(bit_length)
% Generate a random prime number of specified bit length
while true
    % Generate a random odd number of given bit length
    p = randi([2^(bit_length - 1), 2^bit_length - 1]);
    if mod(p, 2) == 0
        p = p + 1;
    end
    if isprime_miller_rabin(p, 5)  % 5 rounds is sufficient for demonstration
        return;
    end
end
end
```

